      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We begin by assuming that $x = y$. Let $a = x^2 + y$. Then,\n\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\left(2^4\\right)^a + \\left(2^4\\right)^a &= 1 \\\\\n2^{4a} + 2^{4a} &= 1 \\\\\n2^{4a} (1 + 1) &= 1 \\\\\n2^{4a} \\cdot 2 &= 1 \\\\\n2^{4a + 1} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\\]\nthen we have,\n\\[\\begin{aligned}\n4a + 1 &= 0 \\\\\n4a &= -1 \\\\\na &= \\boxed{-\\frac{1}{4}}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]\nSo the solutions are of the form $x = y = \\sqrt{-\\frac{1}{4}}$.",
